WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.834
-Aspiring
Republican politicians,

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.567
from David Perdue in Georgia
to J.D. Vance in Ohio,

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:08.000
have decided the path to power
in their party

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.033
requires fully embracing
Donald Trump

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.834
and his lies
about the 2020 election,

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:13.767
even as more damning
evidence emerges

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.000
about Trump's attempted coup.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.167
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:21.501
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:24.367
We keep getting more bombshell
text messages

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.400
implicating more members
of Trump's inner circle

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.701
in the attempt to overturn
the 2020 election results

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.200
and today, a new batch
of text messages revealed

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.033
this message from Trump's
advisor and daughter Ivanka

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.567
to a group chat
of Trump's closest advisors

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.567
two days after the election.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:41.901
-On November 5th,
Ivanka Trump texted Meadows

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.734
and the group...

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:53.000
-She's trying to overturn
the results of an election

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.100
with the tone
of a Peloton instructor.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.968
[ Laughter ]
[ Bright singsong ]
You are all warriors

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.968
of epic proportions!

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.767
Let's crank up
that resistance to 30

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.334
and ride to some Fall Out Boy!

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.767
Also, just a tip --
if you're planning a coup,

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.901
maybe don't do it
via group chat?

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:23.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.367
Then there's House GOP Leader
Kevin McCarthy,

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.701
who denied a report last week
that he said

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:30.400
he would urge Trump to resign
after the insurrection

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.467
and then, he was caught on tape

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.467
saying he would urge Trump
to resign.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.667
Putting everything else aside,

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.100
how do these guys
keep getting caught on tape,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.634
lying or contradicting
themselves?

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.167
Donald Trump, Giuliani,
Michael Cohen, Kevin McCarthy --

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.968
they all have tapes.
Is everyone in pro-Trump circles

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:47.868
so paranoid that they're
constantly wearing microphones

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.934
strapped to their heads?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:52.167
Unfortunately,
aspiring Republicans
still clearly believe

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.300
that the path to success
in their party

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.367
goes straight through Trump.

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:57.067
Most of them are open about it

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.868
and don't care how ridiculous
it makes them look.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.467
For example,
here's Senator Lindsey Graham,

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:05.534
on January 6, 2021,
the day of the insurrection,

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:08.901
versus Lindsey Graham last week
on Fox News.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:12.167
-Trump and I, we've had
a hell of a journey.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.801
I hate it being this way.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.467
Oh, my God, I hate it.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.234
From my point of view, he's been
a consequential president.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:22.267
But today,
first thing you'll see.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:25.734
All I can say is count me out.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.167
Enough is enough.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.334
Donald Trump
is the leader of this party,

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.167
not Kevin McCarthy,
not Lindsey Graham,

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.534
not Newt Gingrich.
-Based on the

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.434
America First agenda.
-I'm hoping soon he --

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:38.934
-Yeah, I'm hoping, soon, he will
lay out a positive agenda.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.968
-[ As Graham ] That's it.
I've had enough of this guy.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.868
Enough to prove to me
that he is the future

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:45.067
of the Republican Party.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.033
Also, I'm sorry,
you're hoping Donald Trump

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.234
will lay out
a positive agenda now?

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.100
Because everyone knows
you radically

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.234
change your personality
when you hit the age of 75.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.033
When I turn 75,
I'm going to drop everything,

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.901
move to Santa Monica,
dye my hair bleach blond

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:59.133
and become one of those jacked,
shirtless dudes

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.367
that do sit-ups
by the pier at 5:00 am.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:04.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.200
I just want to stipulate

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.400
that I gave the graphics
department free rein

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.801
[ Laughter ]
to do whatever they wanted
with that photo

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.534
and, as usual,
they decided to [bleep] me.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:18.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.501
That's not a sit-up!

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:23.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.367
But seriously, what is wrong
with these guys?

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.601
Trump already ran for president,
was president,

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:32.367
ran for president again,
staged a coup to stay in power,

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.801
and never once changed
through any of that.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.968
You think now he's going
to wake up one day,

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.234
look in the mirror, and say --

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.334
[ As Trump ]
You know what?
Instead of trying

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:41.167
to overthrow democracy,
I should sit down

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.167
and come up with a detailed
infrastructure plan.

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:44.334
[ English accent ]
Eric!

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:47.067
Fetch me my inkwell
and my thinking slippers.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.467
I have an English accent
now, too, Eric.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:51.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.067
I'm a new man.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:56.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.033
It's also both funny
and depressing,

00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:02.100
how definitive Trump toadies
were on January 6th

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.501
and how quickly
they backed down.

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:06.467
Lindsey Graham would've made
such a [bleep] Braveheart.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:07.767
[ As Graham ]
They may take our lives,

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:09.267
but they will never
take our freedom.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.534
But also, I think
I might have a way for us

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:13.200
to get both our lives
and our freedom,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.968
and that's to listen
to these British fellows

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.167
because they're not all bad.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:17.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:19.400
Republicans are all desperate
to please Trump

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.801
and willing
to debase themselves

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.868
in the most humiliating ways
possible in order to do it,

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:26.567
like when Texas Senator Ted Cruz
committed the grave GOP sin --

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.634
calling the insurrection
a violent terrorist attack --

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.267
then got criticized
by Tucker Carlson
for saying that,

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.300
then had to go
on Tucker's show the next day

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.267
to grovel
and beg for his forgiveness,

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:38.334
while Tucker embarrassed Cruz
with a chyron that said...

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.567
[ Laughter ]
First of all, you couldn't think
of something better

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:43.601
than that,
Cruz'ing for a bruising?

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.067
I mean, that's been done,
my man.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.734
You got to do something like
"You Cruz, you lose,"

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:47.968
or "Carnival Cruz"
or, I don't know,

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.467
"Clear eyes, full hearts,
can't Cruz."

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:50.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:51.667
These are just pitches.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:52.767
It's brainstorming.

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:53.734
There are no bad ideas.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.467
Well...I guess, going to Cancún

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.400
[ Booing ]
when your home state
suffered a weather emergency.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.834
That's a bad idea.
That right there is a bad idea.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:02.167
I guess, if you really wanted
to embarrass Ted Cruz,

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.434
you could also just cut off
the electricity

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:05.868
to his house
during a snowstorm

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:08.868
and see which exotic tourist
destination he flies to next.

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.267
"And now Senator Ted Cruz

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:12.334
joins us from the Cinnabon
in Terminal 4 at JFK,

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:15.033
where he's waiting for his
connection to Monte Carlo."

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:17.000
[ As Cruz ]
I stand with the people
of Texas.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.501
Oh, wait, hold on.

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.767
They just called my group.
I got to board.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:23.267
Aspiring Republican politicians
clearly think

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:24.968
this is what they have
to do to succeed --

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:27.734
please Trump, embrace his
authoritarian ambitions,

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.634
and repeat his lies
about the 2020 election.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:32.400
Like former Georgia Senator
David Perdue,

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.534
who lost to current
Democratic Senator Jon Ossoff

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:38.300
in a runoff election
in January 2021.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.534
Perdue is now running against

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:41.267
incumbent Republican
Governor Brian Kemp,

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:44.167
as a full pro-Trump
election liar

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:47.367
who blames his own loss
on nonexistent voter fraud

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:50.267
and opened a debate with Kemp
last night by saying this.

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:53.868
-First off, folks,
let me be very clear tonight.

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:57.234
The election in 2020
was rigged and stolen.

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:59.400
Our governor caved
and allowed radical Democrats

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.467
to steal our election.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:02.868
And because of that,

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:04.934
he has divided our party
and cannot win.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:07.767
He sold us out
and cost us the majority

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.033
in the United States Senate.

00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:12.400
I'm proud to have
President Trump's endorsement.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.000
-Wow.
That was like watching Helly

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.167
read the break room apology
on "Severance."

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:19.300
Too soon to reference
"Severance" in "A Closer Look"?

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.434
We talk about the show a lot
in the office,

00:06:21.434 --> 00:06:23.467
but we do want to make sure
you, the audience,

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:25.133
are caught up enough
to enjoy the reference.

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:27.300
I will say,
based on the absence of noise,

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.501
I'm going to say no, but --

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:31.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.501
I've been in the business
a while.

00:06:33.501 --> 00:06:34.734
I tend to have an ear...

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:37.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:38.934
...for this sort of thing.

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:42.434
But do, do, please go to...

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:43.834
...on Twitter, you know,

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:45.567
before you know who
shuts it down...

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:48.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.367
...where the options will be...

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:55.267
Look, I don't want to talk
about this anymore.

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:58.601
There's also this great moment
in Perdue's opening statement.

00:06:58.601 --> 00:07:00.367
-What you're going to see
tonight, unfortunately,

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:03.334
is an embattled governor,

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:06.167
a career politician --
20-year career politician --

00:07:06.167 --> 00:07:08.400
who's going to parrot
his political handlers

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.834
to distract you
away from the fact

00:07:09.834 --> 00:07:12.567
that he sold us out
and cost us the majority

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:13.701
in the United States Senate.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:15.100
-"Career politician."

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.534
Just a reminder -- this guy was
a senator for six years

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.434
and then tried to do it
for another six years,

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:20.400
but lost his election.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.534
The only reason he's not also

00:07:22.534 --> 00:07:23.634
a career politician is

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:24.834
he's just not good at it.

00:07:24.834 --> 00:07:26.467
[ Laughter ]
It's like Johnny Manziel

00:07:26.467 --> 00:07:27.968
snidely calling Tom Brady

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:29.534
a "career football player."

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:30.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:32.133
Also, let me see
if I get this straight.

00:07:32.133 --> 00:07:35.234
Perdue lost to Ossoff
in a runoff in January 2021,

00:07:35.234 --> 00:07:37.567
two months after the general
election in November 2020,

00:07:37.567 --> 00:07:39.634
so his theory is that,
while Donald Trump

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:41.067
and the entirety
of the Republican Party

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:42.133
were screaming their heads off,

00:07:42.133 --> 00:07:43.534
claiming the election
was stolen,

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:46.801
Democrats were able to secretly
rig a second election

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:48.400
without anyone noticing.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.934
So, when Rudy Giuliani
was flying across the country,

00:07:50.934 --> 00:07:52.334
leaking like a busted muffler,

00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:54.234
[ Laughter ]
and Republicans were
scanning ballots

00:07:54.234 --> 00:07:56.868
for secret watermarks
and bamboo fibers from China,

00:07:56.868 --> 00:07:59.767
they just missed the piles
of fraudulent ballots

00:07:59.767 --> 00:08:01.334
being dumped out
of trucks labeled what?

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:04.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.501 --> 00:08:06.567
Republicans have made it clear
they will debase themselves

00:08:06.567 --> 00:08:08.000
in the most humiliating
ways possible

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.767
to slink back to Trump
and earn his support,

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:12.067
like over the weekend,
when Trump rallied

00:08:12.067 --> 00:08:13.934
with Ohio Senate
candidate J.D. Vance.

00:08:13.934 --> 00:08:16.400
Vance relentlessly
criticized Trump in public

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.701
and even suggested Trump could
potentially be America's Hitler,

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:21.133
in a recently unearthed message,

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:24.567
but has now come crawling back
to win Trump's endorsement,

00:08:24.567 --> 00:08:26.200
by mindlessly parroting

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.200
his various lies
and conspiracy theories.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.934
-Ladies and gentlemen,
the thing that Trump revealed,

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:32.968
more than any
policy achievement,

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:34.133
is that we are living

00:08:34.133 --> 00:08:36.534
in an incredibly
corrupt country.

00:08:36.534 --> 00:08:39.100
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.567
[ Whistling ]

00:08:40.567 --> 00:08:43.667
Who would've believed that the
Federal Bureau of Investigation,

00:08:43.667 --> 00:08:45.100
our FBI,

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:48.601
would have got an illegal
wiretap on a U.S. president?

00:08:48.601 --> 00:08:50.534
-I mean, no one,
because it didn't happen.

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:52.167
Well, not no one,
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.167 --> 00:08:53.701
because there are people
in the crowd

00:08:53.701 --> 00:08:55.701
who believe it, I guess,
the same way there are

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:58.000
at least a few people
at WWE shows

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.400
who think the moves are real.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.734
[ Laughter ]
"Holy [bleep].

00:09:00.734 --> 00:09:02.300
That dude just got hit
on the head

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.534
with a plastic folding chair
and didn't even flinch.

00:09:04.534 --> 00:09:07.267
Also, why do they keep those
chairs so close to the ring?

00:09:07.267 --> 00:09:09.767
[ Laughter ]
And now, The Rock
is cooking something?

00:09:09.767 --> 00:09:11.400
I didn't know he was a chef."

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.334
These guys just make [bleep] up

00:09:14.334 --> 00:09:15.601
and don't even bother
to explain it

00:09:15.601 --> 00:09:17.400
with made-up details
because they don't have to.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.434
They say they're done
with Trump on January 6th,

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:21.667
only to change their mind?
Their base doesn't care.

00:09:21.667 --> 00:09:23.601
They claim they never
said something,

00:09:23.601 --> 00:09:25.067
only for a tape to prove
they're lying?

00:09:25.067 --> 00:09:26.501
Fox News doesn't cover it.

00:09:26.501 --> 00:09:28.133
They say the FBI wiretapped
the president,

00:09:28.133 --> 00:09:29.634
without proof?
The crowd cheers.

00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:31.367
Because their base
supports Donald Trump,

00:09:31.367 --> 00:09:33.601
the flip-floppingest,
most truth-allergic,

00:09:33.601 --> 00:09:36.367
evidence-free human being
who ever stood at a podium

00:09:36.367 --> 00:09:37.901
and bitched about toilets.

00:09:37.901 --> 00:09:39.701
[ Laughter and applause ]
So, of course,
Vance and all his allies

00:09:39.701 --> 00:09:40.701
have come slinking back.

00:09:40.701 --> 00:09:42.033
They've come slinking back
to Trump

00:09:42.033 --> 00:09:44.467
and Trump is aware of the power
he wields over them

00:09:44.467 --> 00:09:47.200
and he seems to enjoy
reminding them of it

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.801
and humiliating them with it,

00:09:48.801 --> 00:09:51.334
as he did with Vance
over the weekend.

00:09:51.334 --> 00:09:54.834
-I'm very pleased to introduce
the man with, by far,

00:09:54.834 --> 00:09:58.234
the best chance to defeat
the radical Democrat nominee

00:09:58.234 --> 00:10:00.701
for the U.S. Senate
this November.

00:10:00.701 --> 00:10:02.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:10:02.734 --> 00:10:04.467
And you know what?
You know what?

00:10:04.467 --> 00:10:07.300
He's the guy that said
some bad [bleep] about me.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:09.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.234
-Yeah!

00:10:11.234 --> 00:10:12.901
-He did.

00:10:12.901 --> 00:10:14.200
[ Whistling ]
But you know what?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.534
Every one of the others
did also.

00:10:16.534 --> 00:10:18.367
Fact, if I went
by that standard,

00:10:18.367 --> 00:10:20.300
I don't think I would've
ever endorsed anybody

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.834
in the country,
you want to know.

00:10:21.834 --> 00:10:23.200
-[ As Trump ]
So many people said

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.667
so much bad [bleep] about me.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:28.000
Every one of them,
top to bottom, no exceptions.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.267
You know, it's really --

00:10:29.267 --> 00:10:30.634
It's almost like
they were right.

00:10:30.634 --> 00:10:32.033
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:34.434
I mean, if that many people said
that much bad [bleep] about you,

00:10:34.434 --> 00:10:36.334
at some point,
you might start to think that,

00:10:36.334 --> 00:10:37.300
"Maybe I'm a bad guy."

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.868 --> 00:10:40.033
It's funny.

00:10:40.033 --> 00:10:42.834
Anyway, toilets
don't flush anymore.

00:10:42.834 --> 00:10:44.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:44.434 --> 00:10:46.701
I do love that he
constantly reminds

00:10:46.701 --> 00:10:49.234
